      "id": 1,
      "text": "Holiday Beach began as a planned community when Dallas investors formed the Copano Land Company in the mid‑1960s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/holiday-beach-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first lots went on sale in January 1964, marking the start of the town’s residential development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/holiday-beach-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Over the next decades, Holiday Beach grew with waterfront homes and a network of boat canals that still define its layout.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/holiday-beach-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By 1990 the community had about 1,000 residents, a number that remained steady through the 2000 census.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/holiday-beach-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In August 2017, Hurricane Harvey struck Holiday Beach, causing extensive damage to homes and infrastructure.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
